    "kind": "analysis",
    "text": "# Investigation note: metric M314650, reporting month 2026-10-31\n\n**1. Executive finding**\nM314650 is in the provisional **Amber (watch)** band and is not healthy. The provisional rate is 56.5% (26 of 46), up 3.5 percentage points from the month before. That is about 3.5 points below the provisional red threshold of 60%. It is the highest rate since 2025-11-30 (64.3%). Most of this month's change comes from application-level churn: 12 newly non-compliant and 13 resolved. Applications joining and leaving the metric also contributed.\n\n**2. Current status and period (2026-10-31)**\n- Provisional rate 0.565217: numerator 26, denominator 46.\n- There are 64 metric rows, from 64 distinct applications. 20 rows are Non_Compliant, 26 Compliant, 13 Pending and 5 Not_Applicable.\n- The denominator leaves out Pending rows (inferred, an assumption), which is why it is 46 and not 64.\n\n**3. Movement against 2026-09-30 (provisional)**\n- The rate went from 0.530612 (26 of 49) to 0.565217.\n- **Composition:**\n  - 55 applications reported in both months. Their rate went from 22 of 41 (53.7%) to 22 of 40 (55.0%).\n  - 9 applications reported only in October, contributing 4 of 6.\n  - 12 applications reported only in September, contributing 4 of 8.\n- **Movement among the 55 continuing applications:** 12 newly non-compliant, 6 persistently non-compliant, 13 resolved and 24 other. The 9 new applications include 2 non-compliant rows, which brings the total to 20.\n- **Over 12 months:** the rate ranged from 42.3% (2026-01-31) to 64.3% (2025-11-30). It has stayed in the amber range since 2026-02-28.\n**4. Biggest contributors (non-compliant rows, business organisation hierarchy)**\n- **Super_Division_05:** 5 of its 10 rows.\n- **Super_Division_04:** 4 of 15.\n- **Super_Division_02:** 4 of 9.\n- **Super_Division_03 and Super_Division_07:** 2 each, out of 5 rows each.\n- **Super_Division_01, _06 and _08:** 1 each.\n- **Legal entities:** the non-compliant rows are spread out. No legal entity has more than 2 (Legal_Entity_39, _22, _03 and _04 have 2 each). No single legal entity or application dominates.\n**5. Testing and exception observations (observed data)**\n- **Failed tests:** 14 of the 20 non-compliant rows are completed tests that failed. The reasons given are Open_Findings_Outstanding (6), Test_Failed (5) and Remediation_Overdue (3).\n- **No test or overdue test:** 5 non-compliant rows. 4 have No_Test (Test_Overdue 2, No_Test_Performed 2) and 1 is Test_Pending and overdue.\n- **Odd combinations:**\n  - 1 row is Non_Compliant even though its test passed (Open_Findings_Outstanding).\n  - 1 row is Compliant even though its test failed (Compensating_Control_Accepted).\n  - 1 completed test is Compliant but has no result recorded.\n- **Pending and exempt rows (not in the denominator):** 13 Pending rows (Test_Scheduled 4, Test_In_Progress 3, Awaiting_Test_Assignment 3, Result_Under_Review 3) and 5 Not_Applicable rows (3 Exemption_Approved, 2 No_Test_Required).\n\n**6. Areas for further investigation (these are hypotheses, not confirmed causes)**\n- **Which way the band runs.** In this data the numerator counts exactly the Compliant rows (26 of 26). The supplied band says a higher rate is worse, which would mean more compliant rows is worse. That needs to be checked with the client before the Amber status is relied on.\n- **Churn.** Find out why 12 continuing applications became non-compliant while 13 resolved.\n- **Pending rows.** Check whether the 13 Pending rows, especially the 3 Result_Under_Review, could move the rate when they are resolved.\n- **Super_Division_05 and Super_Division_02.** Each has about half or more of its rows non-compliant, but these are small groups (10 and 9 rows).\n- **Data quality.** The three odd test/status combinations above should be confirmed.\n\n**7. Limitations**\n- The rate, the band, the denominator scope and the movement classifications are all provisional. The client has not confirmed what the numerator and denominator mean.\n- No metric name, family, severity or target is available.\n- The organisation counts are row counts on small bases.\n- The number of applications in the metric changes from month to month, so part of the change reflects who reported rather than performance.\n- Owners, causes and remediation are not shown in the data, and none are implied here.",
